-- `()` is written `⊤` (language.md §12.10): `unit_spelling_removed` at
-- every `()` — in a type (5:5), a pattern (6:3), an expression (6:10) — and
-- at a `( )` with a space (10:11), each from its `(` to its `)`; the parse
-- goes on as `⊤`, so nothing else is reported.
f : () → Int
f () = g ()


g : ⊤ → Int
g u = h u ( )


h : ⊤, ⊤ → Int
h a b = 0
